<title>LATVIA: KAIJA, RIGA ALUS SHAREHOLDERS BUY STATE SHARES.</title>
<headline>KAIJA, RIGA ALUS SHAREHOLDERS BUY STATE SHARES.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The privatisation agency said on Wednesday that it has allowed the shareholders of Kaija and Rigas alus to buy the state's stakes in the company.</p>
<p>Kaija shareholders are to buy 504,377 state-owned shares at 1.25 lats, the average for the last quarter of 1996 on the bourse, while Rigas alus shareholders will purchase 412,272 shares at one lat, the agency said in a statement.</p>
<p>The shares were created as the companies capitalised their debts.</p>
<p>The companies can decide whether to issue the new shares on the bourse or retain them.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
